Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.20 Cheats screen, page 2: Warp (DW3_CHEATS builds only)

The Warp row picks an area of the stage select (Asuka City, the Digimon Lab,
the Arena, Central Park, the Wire Forest, Tyranno Valley, the four cities, the
Bulk Swamp, the Noise Desert and Snow Mountain). At the first idle frame of
the field after it was armed (patch 0118's place), the field leaves for that
mode with argument 0 (FIELDSTG_leaveField(mode, 0, 0, 0, 0)): the stage's first
start point, which is what the debug stage select does (requestMode(mode, 0))
and what a story exit slot does with its own argument. The field closes as
for an exit, so the game is in the same state as after walking there: it can
be saved (the field menu records the place) and played. Logs
"dw3: P6.20 cheat warp from mode=0x.. to mode=0x..".

Every line is inside #ifdef DW3_CHEATS.

--- a/src/field/field_mode/field.c
+++ b/src/field/field_mode/field.c
@@ -515,6 +515,21 @@
                         fprintf(stderr, "dw3: P6.20 cheat item %d %d -> %d\n", (int)cheatId, (int)have,
                                 (int)GAME.items[cheatId]);
                     }
+                }
+            }
+#endif
+#ifdef DW3_CHEATS
+            /* P6.20 Warp: leaves for the armed area like an exit slot does, with
+               argument 0 (the stage's first start), as the debug stage select
+               requests a field (requestMode(mode, 0)) */
+            {
+                s32 cheatMode;
+
+                if (dw3_cheats_take_warp(&cheatMode)) {
+                    fprintf(stderr, "dw3: P6.20 cheat warp from mode=0x%x to mode=0x%x\n",
+                            (unsigned)GAME.funcs.getMode(), (unsigned)cheatMode);
+                    FIELDSTG_leaveField(cheatMode, 0, 0, 0, 0);
+                    break;
                 }
             }
 #endif
